# Private markers and intermediates must be consumed with the sequence.
# A parser that bails on '>' '$' or '!' prints the final byte as text, which is
# what made modern TUIs show stray q/p characters on startup.
size: 20x3
description: private-marker and intermediate CSI sequences print nothing

--- input
\e[>q\e[?2026$p\e[!p\e[>4;2mAB

--- expect-grid
|AB|
||
||

--- expect-cursor
row=0 col=2
